{
 "comment": "MyPaint brush file",
 "version": 3,
 "description": "Erode",
 "notes": "TOOL, operator `erode` (rapier_op 6). Wear, from the edges in: coverage is pulled toward the smallest coverage in its own neighbourhood, so a mark frays where it already borders emptiness and its interior does not move however long the hand scrubs. Drag it across the middle of a solid patch and nothing happens -- that is the difference between eroding and erasing. Surviving colour is exact.\n\nWhat an artist reaches for it to do, and its whole contract: docs/paint-tools.md.\n\nAuthor: Rapier\nLicense: AGPL-3.0-only",
